 if(type==4){y+=paragraph("Save a selected floor area as a named process plan. Plans preserve machine settings, port directions, side-stream branches, utility networks and walls; stamping never copies food.",x,y,body.width,12,fMuted)+12;button({x,y,body.width-94,32},planName.empty()?"Name this process plan":planName,[this]{editFocus=4;},editFocus==4,true,"Type a name for the next plan, or select Rename beside a saved plan",{},11);button({x+body.width-88,y,88,32},planRenameIndex>=0?"Save name":"Capture area",[this]{if(planRenameIndex>=0){factory.setPlanName(size_t(planRenameIndex),planName);planRenameIndex=-1;planName.clear();}else{factoryCopying=true;factoryStamp.reset();factoryErasing=false;factoryOverlay=0;factory.notice="Drag a rectangle around the complete process, including side routes and utility lines, to save it as a plan.";}},false,planRenameIndex>=0?!planName.empty():true,planRenameIndex>=0?"Apply the new name to this saved plan":"Close Plans, then drag a floor area to capture its actual machines and routes",fOrange,9.5f);y+=39;button({x,y,body.width,32},"Glass lab apparatus",[this]{factoryStamp=Factory::glassLabBlueprint();factoryTab=0;factoryErasing=factoryCopying=false;factoryOverlay=0;},false,true,"Place a real glass apparatus with equal-length feeds, a Y-mixer, burette, heated flask, condenser, coil, stopcock and receiving beaker",{},11);y+=38;button({x,y,body.width,32},"Fractional distillation train",[this]{factoryStamp=Factory::fractionalDistillationBlueprint();factoryTab=0;factoryErasing=factoryCopying=false;factoryOverlay=0;},false,true,"Stamp a three-cut train with adjustable reflux columns, real condensers and separate fraction receivers",{},11);y+=42;for(size_t i=0;i<factory.blueprints.size();i++){auto& bp=factory.blueprints[i];float nameW=body.width-83;button({x,y,nameW,31},bp.name,[this,i]{factoryStamp=factory.blueprints[i];factoryTab=0;factoryErasing=factoryCopying=false;factoryOverlay=0;},false,std::none_of(bp.parts.begin(),bp.parts.end(),[](const BlueprintPart& p){return p.machine.kind==MachineKind::RecipeKitchen;}),"Stamp this saved process plan on empty floor",{},10.5f);button({x+nameW+5,y,78,31},"Rename",[this,i]{planRenameIndex=int(i);planName=factory.blueprints[i].name;editFocus=4;},false,true,"Rename this saved plan",{},9.5f);y+=37;}}
 else if(type==2){for(int i=0;i<int(factoryRequests().size());i++){auto& r=factoryRequests()[i];button({x,y,body.width,32},r.name,[this,i]{factory.setRequest(i);factoryOverlay=0;},factory.request==i,true,r.description,{},12);y+=39;y+=paragraph(r.description,x,y,body.width,11,fMuted)+13;}}
 else{for(auto& p:std::vector<std::string>{"The western power district supplies actual electricity to the farm and molecular works. Power in the toolbar centres it on this same floor. Solar arrays generate DC; batteries need an inverter to supply AC. Wind, steam and gas engines drive alternators through shafts. Drag matching cables or pipes beneath equipment, then inspect ports, live flow, reserves, trip heat and output history. Right-click selects; a conduit brush can select its layer beneath a machine.","Boilers burn real organic food and need makeup water. Condensers return turbine exhaust as water. Digesters remove compounds from actual leftovers, scrubbers clean the gas, and engines recover heat. Route ash and digestate from the side outlet to compost. Heat pipes can supply heaters; a recovery cooling plant supplies chillers. Batteries and flywheels have finite reserves, rates and standing losses. Relay thresholds dispatch reserve engines. Critical/Normal/Optional priorities decide shortages; mixers and heaters can run slowly on partial supply. Isolate a hot route, allow it to cool, then reset its breaker. Plans preserve this entire arrangement without copying food or stored energy.","All cooking happens on the floor. Feeders supply measured ingredients; mixers, dosers and processing machines change the real batches moving between them. There is no separate test plate or instant processing menu.","Search glass to build transparent tubing, residence coils, stopcocks, heated flasks, cooling condensers, burettes, Y-mixers and receiving beakers. Drag glass tubing to connect stages; R turns its outlet. Plans includes Glass lab apparatus with two measured feeds and a complete real process. A beaker can hold, serve or forward actual food.","Fractional distillation is a real three-stream process. A still boils a selected heads, hearts or tails cut into its clockwise side outlet and sends the stillage onward. A reflux column enriches vapour by volatility and returns a water-rich stream to the still. The condenser changes that vapour into liquid; collect and name each cut in its own fraction receiver. Plans has a complete three-cut train.","Start with the experiment cell below the sample factory, or place one with Cell. Its two feeders start in single mode. Select a feeder, set its ingredient and grams from the pantry, then Dispense once.","The mixer waits for both inputs. Run or Step the shared clock to move and process the batches. Adjust dwell, target temperature and shear on the actual selected machine. Use a component plater when separate textures should remain distinct.","The experiment cell's tasting dock holds its output. Inspect the live composition, taste, compound masses and process history. Enter a name and Record dish from that dock's actual batch. Automatic docks retain their latest serving as a read-only record.","Build line stamps the actual contributing machines, with feeder doses, machine settings and side routes. Feeders and the final tasting dock become automatic for production. Saved references without a floor layout cannot create food.","A dock can hold, serve automatically, or forward batches to connected machines. Cycle Audience between Restaurant pass, Research tasting and Chilled pickup. Restaurant docks score the active optional ticket against phase, compounds, temperature and quality; matched servings build a timed streak and missed targets include suggestions. Research consumes a sample and logs composition plus process clues without sales or ticket pressure. Chilled pickup accepts only food at 8 C or colder and keeps warm batches held for chilling. Serve points stay outside factory areas, including a one-tile wall opening filled by the dock or a conveyor. Recent Service and each dock's last report keep the results visible.","Flow (V) shows actual batch transfers, molecular structures and measured changes on the floor. Select or hover a machine for its live food and last measured effect. Pause holds both the food and its state; transfer traces finish the last actual move. Wheel zoom reveals finer structures. Space runs or pauses; period steps. Wheel zooms smoothly around the pointer; middle-drag, Alt-left-drag or right-drag pans; right-click selects a machine. R rotates, Q captures a plan, B opens plans, Home frames a readable working area around the selected line and F fits all machines. Typing captures keyboard shortcuts.","Place Factory wall tiles from the build library and drag a continuous perimeter. A closed wall loop tints its enclosed floor as a factory area; untinted open floor remains outside. Wall tiles occupy floor cells and block batch routes. Tasting docks inside a factory area cannot serve; put each one outside the perimeter or in a straight wall opening.","Machines have visible ports: cyan marks inputs, dark teal the main outlet, and orange the clockwise side stream. The inspector names each connected neighbour. Point a separator's side stream into another process to recover useful fractions instead of letting them block the line.","Build Utility stations and matching coloured Utility lines. A station and its connected lines share a per-tick capacity; adjacent processes tap that service. A station activates the constraint: unconnected or overloaded processes that need that service pause. Heat and cooling demand follows the machine's target; water and vacuum are used by processes that need them. Factory input buffers deplete in every mode: powered processes use electricity, machines with a water demand use process water, Produce and Dairy ingredients draw farm produce, and Agent ingredients draw chemicals. Use Factory Inputs in the inspector for direct deliveries; these cost nothing in Free Build and are priced in Economy. The northern farm and western power district provide real upstream production. Direct deliveries remain available as an optional fallback; a metered grid inlet must connect imported electricity to a physical AC circuit. Utility lines are an optional separate constraint; Economy adds grid capacity and operating fees.","Place a pH probe, temperature logger, droplet microscope or aroma sensor beside a batch and rotate the instrument toward it. Each samples real batch state once per tick, shows its current batch identity, and keeps a short reading history so you can compare changes along a process.","Open Plans, type a name, choose Capture area, then drag around the whole process. Include side outlets and utility lines. The saved plan keeps machine settings, directions and routes; stamp it elsewhere to reuse the arrangement without copying food.","Separators preserve both fractions. Route the clockwise side outlet so a blocked by-product cannot stop production. Free Build removes pantry stock, grid-capacity and cash limits, while electricity, water, farm-produce and chemical buffers still deplete. Utility networks you build still use their shared rated capacity.","Chemistry is a stylised game model: pH, water activity, hydrocolloids, enzymes, culture metabolism, fat droplets, foam, ice and thermal history influence what the real machines produce."})y+=paragraph(p,x,y,body.width,12,fMuted)+15;}
 modalContentHeight=y-start+300-body.height;endClip();
